% =============================================================================
% will — Weighted Intuitionistic Linear Logic (TODO_0292 / TODO_0297)
% =============================================================================
%
% The measure-class calculus (THY_0026): gill's graded surface, read under
% the unnormalized measure semiring (ℚ≥0, ·, +) — weights multiply along a
% derivation, alternatives aggregate by sum (exact mass) or PRF sample,
% never by an order prune. The surface is INHERITED, not copied: @extends
% gill is the first cross-calculus chain (meta-parser loadChain merges the
% constructor and sort-edge tables), so will declares only what is
% will-OWN — and at P0 that is nothing. woplus, the graded monad/bang,
% haul, stamps and windows all arrive from gill; the ∃_ρ graded
% existential (M1) and @w constructor priors land in later phases.
%
% Weight discipline (D5): woplus grades stay fenced to [0,1] — THY_0021's
% normalized binary reading is unchanged. Unnormalized ℚ≥0 masses enter as
% @w PRIOR annotations on constructors, renormalized when a superposition
% expands (ratios in, probabilities out); the weight SORT never widens.

@family will.
@extends gill.

% ∃_ρ — the weight-graded existential (M1, P3). Surface `exists X: s @w. A`
% parses (will-only binder rule) to superpose(s, exists(A)): the sort
% names the domain whose constructor-declared @w weights grade the
% choice; the inner exists carries the de Bruijn binder (kernel binder
% machinery untouched). A suspended superpose-fact IS the wave — plain
% settle leaves it inert; the decimation driver collapses it (D4: plain
% `exists X. A` stays a skolem even under the driver).
% The spelled @ascii form exists for will.rules PATTERNS (`superpose S
% (exists X. A)` — sequent rules match on it, TODO_0298 item 1); writing
% it directly in a program is legal and identical to the binder sugar.
% NO @polarity annotation: like `at`, superpose stays unpolarized at the
% SEARCH level — its right rule (∃_ρ-R = will.rules drawn_l) is
% mechanically a left rule on the token, which strict right-focus could
% never reach. The focused system's assignment (∃_ρ positive, THY_0027
% §8) is the paper's canonical COUNTING discipline, not this engine's
% search heuristic.
superpose: sort -> formula -> formula
  @ascii "superpose #1 #2".

% Draw token (THY_0027 §1) — the kernel-reserved trace hypothesis:
% `drawn c s` is the linear record "a draw of member c at sort s
% occurred". The member slot is dependently (c : s) — checked by the
% @draw checker and the drawn_l theory, never by the grammar; `member`
% is its honest grammar-level label. Tokens are GROUND (rung-2 draws
% record the head constructor only). Kernel-reserved fence: no program
% rule may mention drawn (convert.js validates, like at/fire) — tokens
% enter judgments only at the boundary, minted by the @draw checker.
% Positive left-passive in the paper's focused system (THY_0027 §8);
% unpolarized here like superpose (see above). Its left rules (will.rules
% drawn_l = ∃_ρ-R, drawn_l2 = ghost) are non-invertible.
member: type.
drawn: member -> sort -> formula
  @ascii "drawn #1 #2".
